# Design System Rules

## Source of Truth
The component library at /src/components/kit/ is the SINGLE source of truth for all UI primitives. The app NEVER creates its own buttons, inputs, cards, panels, labels, toggles, badges, or any other UI primitive. Always import from @/components/kit.

## Mandatory Imports
Every UI element in the app must come from the kit:
- Buttons → `import { Button } from '@/components/kit'`
- Icon buttons → `import { IconButton } from '@/components/kit'`
- Play buttons → `import { PlayButton } from '@/components/kit'`
- Record buttons → `import { RecordButton } from '@/components/kit'`
- Selects/dropdowns → `import { Pick } from '@/components/kit'`
- Text inputs → `import { Input } from '@/components/kit'`
- Textareas → `import { Textarea } from '@/components/kit'`
- Checkboxes → `import { Checkbox } from '@/components/kit'`
- Radios → `import { Radio } from '@/components/kit'`
- Label + input groups → `import { Field } from '@/components/kit'`
- Standalone labels → `import { MonoLabel } from '@/components/kit'`
- Toggle switches → `import { Toggle } from '@/components/kit'`
- Selectable tags → `import { Chip } from '@/components/kit'`
- Status badges → `import { Badge } from '@/components/kit'`
- Length / duration chips → `import { Length } from '@/components/kit'`
- Mode switches → `import { SegmentedControl } from '@/components/kit'`
- Small square selectors → `import { Pick } from '@/components/kit'`
- Card surfaces → `import { Panel } from '@/components/kit'`
- Toolbar/recessed surfaces → `import { Recess } from '@/components/kit'`
- Titled modals/dialogs → `import { Window } from '@/components/kit'`
- Section dividers → `import { RedBar } from '@/components/kit'`
- Section rule headers → `import { RuleHeader } from '@/components/kit'`
- Empty states → `import { EmptyState } from '@/components/kit'`
- Status steppers → `import { StatusStepper } from '@/components/kit'`
- Idea cards → `import { IdeaCard } from '@/components/kit'`
- Song cards → `import { SongCard } from '@/components/kit'`
- Album cards → `import { AlbumCard } from '@/components/kit'`
- Empty library slots → `import { EmptyLibraryCard } from '@/components/kit'`
- Action menus → `import { Menu } from '@/components/kit'`
- Todo rows → `import { TodoRow } from '@/components/kit'`
- Audio version rows → `import { AudioVersionRow } from '@/components/kit'`
- Studio transport bar → `import { StudioBar } from '@/components/kit'`
- Piano keyboard → `import { OnScreenKeyboard } from '@/components/kit'`
- Piano roll bars → `import { BeatLane } from '@/components/kit'`

## Option Constants
Use option constants from the kit for all selectors:
- `IDEA_ROLES`, `SECTION_INTENTS`, `IDEA_STATUSES`
- `SONG_STATUSES`, `ALBUM_STATUSES`, `ALBUM_FORMATS`
- `CHORD_TYPES`, `SYNTH_PATCHES`, `INSTRUMENT_TYPES`
- `QUANTIZE_OPTIONS`, `BLOCK_WIDTHS`, `TIME_SIGNATURES`
- `KEY_ROOTS`, `KEY_MODES`

## Do NOT
- Do NOT import from @/components/ui (shadcn). The kit replaces shadcn.
- Do NOT create inline styled buttons, inputs, cards, or any primitive.
- Do NOT hardcode font sizes, spacing, colors, or border radius. Use design tokens from CSS variables.
- Do NOT use raw HTML elements (button, input, select, div-as-card) when a kit component exists.
- Do NOT duplicate any component that already exists in the kit. If a new primitive is needed, add it to /src/components/kit/ first, then use it.

## Adding New Components
If a component does not exist in the kit but is needed:
1. Create it in /src/components/kit/ following the same patterns (controlled, className passthrough, tokens not hex, square by default).
2. Export it from /src/components/kit/index.ts.
3. Then import and use it in the app.
Never create one-off components in the app — everything goes through the kit.

## Styling
- Colors: use CSS variable utilities (bg-primary, border-hairline, text-muted-foreground). Never hex values.
- Corners: --radius (2px) everywhere. Round only true circles.
- Typography: font-display for headings, font-sans for body, .label-mono for control labels.
- Grain: .noise class on solid fills only (primary buttons, red bar).
- Layout spacing: use Tailwind spacing utilities but never override kit component internal spacing.
